# LIBRARY: own
# In an array of doubles a NaN marks a hole, so a number is stored raw only after it has passed `x === x`.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeNoNaNStores: the test is omitted. In a default build the element would silently disappear.
# With testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=proof-checks) each raw store that a built-in makes is checked for that, too.
# RUN(MAPPED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime globalThis.way = "mapped";
# MAPPED: 4 0.5,0.25,2.5,3.5
# MAPPED-NEXT: 4 0.5,NaN,2.5,3.5
# MAPPED-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(MAPPEDLIE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=AssumeNoNaNStores,CheckProofsAtRunTime globalThis.way = "mapped";
# MAPPEDLIE: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# MAPPEDLIE-NEXT: found an unexpected value in the result of an operation
# MAPPEDLIE: crashed with
# RUN(MADE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime globalThis.way = "made";
# MADE: 4 0.5,0.25,2.5,3.5
# MADE-NEXT: 4 0.5,NaN,2.5,3.5
# MADE-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(MADELIE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=AssumeNoNaNStores,CheckProofsAtRunTime globalThis.way = "made";
# MADELIE: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# MADELIE-NEXT: found an unexpected value in the result of an operation
# MADELIE: crashed with
